-- title:
--   Vélu quotient has unit c₄ at a multiplicative prime
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with non-vanishing discriminant $\Delta \neq 0$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \mid W.\Delta$ and $\ell \nmid W.c_4$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $\ell \neq p$, and let $Q$ be a point of the curve $W$ base changed along $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Q}$ and then to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, whose additive order is exactly $p$. Write $Wb$ for that base-changed curve. Then the valuation attached to $A$ of the $c_4$-invariant of the Vélu quotient `Wb.veluQuotient (Wb.oddOrderSummingSet Q (p / 2))` equals $1$, that is, this $c_4$ is a unit at $A$. Here `oddOrderSummingSet Q (p / 2)` is the finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \times \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained as the image of $\{1, \dots, \lfloor p/2 \rfloor\}$ under $k \mapsto$ the affine coordinates of $k \bullet Q$ (the point at infinity being sent to $(0,0)$), and `veluQuotient S` is the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $Wb$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\sum_{P \in S} t_P$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2\sum_{P \in S} t_P - 7\sum_{P \in S} w_P$, for the Vélu quantities $t_P$, $w_P$.
--
--   This is the $c_4$-leg of the statement that the Vélu model of the quotient of $W$ by the cyclic group generated by a point of odd prime order $p$ is again of multiplicative type at a prime $\ell \neq p$ of multiplicative reduction. It is used in the Tate-curve cusp criterion for the quotient, [`ModularCurve.tateCuspCriterion_jQuotVelu`](thm.html#ModularCurve.tateCuspCriterion_jQuotVelu), and in [`WeierstrassCurve.dvd_discriminant_not_dvd_c4_integral_veluQuotient_rescale`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.dvd_discriminant_not_dvd_c4_integral_veluQuotient_rescale).
-- source:
